# Notes
notes = "(!) sega_101.bin (md5): f273555d7d91e8a5a6bfd9bcf066331c|(!) sega_100.bin (md5): 2aba43c2f1526c5e898dfe1cafbfc53a|Built on Ymir's cycle-accurate hardware layer (verbatim upstream).|Requires one Saturn BIOS ROM (place in system directory); any of the listed files works.|BIOS Auto boots a Japan/Asia-only disc with a Japanese BIOS and any other disc with a US/EU one (falls back to any BIOS present); keep one of each region.|Load .bin/.img/.mdf images through their .cue/.ccd/.mds sheet.|Japanese BIOS files (Sega Saturn BIOS v1.00/v1.01 (JAP).bin) are also supported.|Optional Vulkan renderer (64-bit desktop builds): set the video driver to vulkan, then core option Renderer = Vulkan and reload the content; Internal Resolution 2x-4x and VDP1 Upscaling apply at once.|Other video drivers use the software renderer.|Save states are deterministic: run-ahead, rewind and netplay work. Save states carry the BIOS language/settings for the session. For netplay, use the same BIOS, core options and cheats on both machines.|Cheats: the Saturn cheat files of RetroArch's database (Action Replay codes) work. RetroAchievements and cheat search use Beetle Saturn's memory layout.|Controllers per port: Control Pad, 3D Control Pad, Arcade Racer, Mission Stick, Shuttle Mouse, Virtua Gun; analog deadzone, trigger deadzone and mouse sensitivity options.|The King of Fighters '95 and Ultraman need their ROM cartridge dump in the system directory (mpr-18811-mx.ic1, mpr-19367-mx.ic1).|Optional CD Block LLE (work in progress in Ymir) needs the CD Block ROM (cdb106.bin, cdb105.bin or cdb104.bin); validated with cdb106.bin and cdb105.bin; save states, run-ahead, rewind and netplay exact in the tested games (BIOS menu, Sega Rally, Virtua Fighter 2, Burning Rangers, Guardian Heroes, Panzer Dragoon II Zwei).|Note: sega1003.bin (JP v1.003) is NOT supported due to compatibility issues.|Visit https://github.com/coredds/brimir for more information."

description = "Brimir is a libretro core for Sega Saturn emulation, built on Ymir's cycle-accurate hardware layer. Features SIMD-optimized threaded software rendering, an optional Vulkan renderer (VDP1 and VDP2 on the GPU, identical to software at native resolution, internal resolution up to 4x; needs RetroArch's Vulkan video driver), live core option updates, dynamic NTSC/PAL AV timing, SRAM single-source persistence, screen rotation (TATE), compressed versioned save states that keep run-ahead, rewind and netplay exact, Action Replay cheats from RetroArch's database, RetroAchievements (Beetle Saturn's memory layout), all Saturn controller types (3D Control Pad, Arcade Racer, Mission Stick, Shuttle Mouse, Virtua Gun with crosshair), RAM, ROM and backup memory cartridges, Ymir's accuracy options (SH-2 cache, CD Block LLE, SCSP step granularity) and multi-disc support. Ymir's hardware layer stays verbatim upstream; Brimir features are implemented in the bridge layer. Interlaced high-resolution titles can be CPU-bound on slower machines. Active development targets an SH-2 JIT (experimental, opt-in). The core requires a Saturn BIOS ROM to function."
